    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk... i think this is a bit too blunt about the failure. if the donors see \"40%\" in big letters, they're gonna think we're incompetent or that our projects don't actually work. they want to feel like they're investing in a winning cause, not a struggling one. \n\ncan we pivot the language? maybe instead of focusing on the villages we missed, we focus on the progress made or the \"near-total coverage\" of the accessible areas? i need something that doesn't make us look like we're failing. we need them to feel like the success is already happening. can we rephrase the impact stats to be more... impactful?",
